  "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
  "data": {
    "body": "Which of the following four statements about the system\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n& x+3 y+z=1 \\\\\n& 3 x+k y+z=3 \\\\\n& 2 x+6 y+7 z=b\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nare true?\n\nI. The system will have only one solution for any values of $k$ and $b$.\n\nII. If $k=9$ and $b=3$ this system will have no solutions\n\nIII. If $k=9$ and $b=2$ this system will have infinitely many solutions\n\nIV. If $k=7$ this system will have only one solution for any value of $b$",
    "solution": [
      4
    ],
